    "intro_html":  "Trinidadian curry beef starts somewhere most curries do not: you burn the curry powder in hot oil first, on purpose, until it goes dark and nutty. Then the beef goes in, the potatoes go in later, and the whole thing simmers into its own thick gravy. Green seasoning does the rest. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e30 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and 586 calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e$4.26\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
